{"id": "EUVD-2026-98684", "enisaUuid": "9098110c-0ba2-34c0-afd7-b4a209841f1e", "description": "ImageMagick before 7.1.2-33 and 6.9.13-58 contains a heap buffer underwrite vulnerability in DecodeImage() in coders/pict.c on 32-bit builds due to pointer arithmetic overflow. Attackers can supply a crafted PICT file with maximized row, column and bytes-per-line values to bypass bounds checks and write up to 128 controlled bytes below the heap buffer, causing crashes or code execution.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T13:35:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:43:16", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-mqmp-r5jh-jx7w", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/63dde0cf281383ab69432b88305f7dcd6a8ce900", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/c18c5d5fb7f1d87ddbe0a02e9d1207c89b24588c", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/blob/7.1.2-32/coders/pict.c#L503-L540", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/imagemagick-before-7.1.2-33-and-6.9.13-58-heap-buffer-underwrite-in-pict-decoder"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109964", "GHSA-279f-3w5r-54f5"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.36, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b3d268d9-3c97-35d7-b2f1-b362b3b5341a", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "7.0.0-0 <7.1.2-33"}, {"id": "b8a539c3-2e51-3182-8a53-f037e88cd741", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.9.13-58"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f131b10d-be36-31dc-919b-43118024697e", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}], "isExploited": false}